In this case: Proposition 114 set the mandate; technical and advisory groups and public input informed planning; the Colorado Parks and Wildlife Commission made plan decisions; implementation restored wolves. Evaluate process, social, and ecological outcomes separately.

Time: 5 minutes. Source: Gonzalez et al. (2025). Walk from voter mandate to implementation. Pause at each arrow: what would count as evidence that information, recommendations, or public input shaped the next step. Point out how evaluation can inform future planning. The study does not measure ecological effects.


Source: Gonzalez et al. (2025)
